      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-325379",
      ":question/problem": "A sports team wants to estimate the average amount of money each fan spends on food and drinks during a game.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Randomly selecting fans from the ticket sales database and contacting them for the amount they spent.\n2. Surveying fans seated in the front row during the game.\n3. Asking people leaving through the VIP lounge."
